  {
    "id": 283525,
    "ecosystem": "npm",
    "package_name": "document-metadata",
    "version": "100.0.1",
    "status": "MALWARE",
    "release_date": 1756717405,
    "detected_on": 1756717607,
    "last_updated": 1756718586,
    "reasons": [
      "The package defines a postinstall script that automatically runs index.js on install. index.js executes local commands (whoami, hostname), encodes that identifying information into a DNS name, and triggers a lookup to an external OAST domain (oast.fun). That is deliberate, covert exfiltration of system-identifying data during installation; the manifest lacks provenance and the \"security research\" claim does not mitigate the clearly malicious behavior. This is active data theft and therefore malicious.",
      "The code runs local system commands (whoami, hostname), constructs a sanitized identifier from their output, and performs a DNS lookup to a remote oast.fun domain. This is a classic out‑of‑band data exfiltration / beaconing technique (leaking host/user info to an attacker-controlled domain). The combination of dynamic command execution plus an external callback to a suspicious domain shows deliberate malicious behavior (exfiltration/C2), not benign utility code.",
      "Install script in minimal package structure, common in packages designed to execute malicious code."
    ]
  },
